emulator/outputs
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CCFULL-ROM calibration input (python -m emulator.mcmc --config <this file>).
The lines are read in order; blank lines and lines starting with # are
skipped, and everything after line 9 is ignored.  Paths are relative to the
project root.  The experimental data, the training box (the support of the
uniform prior), and the CCFULL point of the model come from its manifest.

 1   name of the trained model, as python -m emulator.train_local --check prints it.
     A local model is meant; a global model also works, but each point costs
     as much as in emulator_rom.in.
 2   training_root it was trained into (line 12 of emulator_train.in).
 3   basis rank: 0 uses the trained rank.  A smaller rank keeps the leading
     POD vectors, as on line 3 of emulator_rom.in.
 4   lowest, highest E_cm in MeV of the measured cross sections used in the
     likelihood.  A local model must hold blocks at all of them.
 5   best fit: Latin-hypercube scan points of the training box, seed, and the
     number of least-squares fits started from the best scan points.  One more
     fit starts from the six parameters of the CCFULL input of the model.
 6   ensemble sampler: walkers (at least 12), pilot steps, production steps,
     seed.  The pilot starts around the best fit and uses the experimental
     errors; the production chain continues it with the emulator error added.
     Both chains are saved every 50 steps; --resume continues a stopped one.
 7   emulator error: points of the pilot chain recomputed with exact CCFULL;
     the RMS of emulator - exact at each energy is added in quadrature to the
     experimental error.  0 = no emulator error.
 8   check: posterior points recomputed with exact CCFULL, then the energy
     grid (first, last, step in MeV) of their exact excitation functions.  A
     step that divides the dE of the barrier distribution (3.33 MeV) keeps
     the three-point formula on the grid.
 9   output directory; every run writes a new timestamped directory in it.
